※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ **A list written out and joined onto a list of an arena puts its elements in as
※ they are**, as a list written out in the arena does: an arena gives nothing
※ back one element at a time, so what lasts as long as it -- what was made in
※ it, text in the image, what the heap holds -- goes in without a copy, and the
※ list written out is never made.  So is an element written over, `l⟦i⟧ ← v`:
※ what it replaces stays where it is until the arena goes.  A document built
※ bottom up -- each array made of the values below it -- is then made once and
※ not copied again at every level it is put into.
※
※ And **what such a body answers is what it made in the arena**: a list the loop
※ joins onto there, a call handed a view whose answer points nowhere, a table
※ written in the arena -- none of them is anything but the arena's, and the
※ answer is the arena's as its signature says.
※
※ What is put in is still a value: a list joined on and changed afterwards
※ leaves what went in as it was.
※
※ And a list of an arena's handed through a writer that recurses, walking a
※ tree by reference in a loop, is handed on as it is and answered as the
※ arena's: what a call in the loop answers is what its signature says, read off
※ it before the loop is lowered -- not everything the loop names.

unit ¤size → ¤idx

let std := ⎕import("std")

type Tree = leaf : u64 | name : str | kids : [Tree]

enum Why:
    empty ;
    odd

※ Why a byte cannot be read: a number read out of the bytes, which is no view
※ of them.
fn why_at(bytes: u8⟦⟧, at: u64 ¤idx) → Why:
    if bytes⟦at⟧ & 1u8 = 1u8: Why.odd else: Why.empty

※ A tree of `levels` levels, each of `width` kids, made bottom up in `a`: every
※ kid joined onto its parent's list as it is.
fn grown(bytes: u8⟦⟧, levels: u64, width: u64, a: &mut arena) → Tree ? Why in a:
    if #bytes = 0:
        return ⊥ Why.empty
    if levels = 0u64:
        return Tree(.leaf ← ⎕widen(bytes⟦0⟧, ⌜u64⌝))
    let kids: mut [Tree] = [] in a
    let seen: mut ⸨u64: u64⸩ = ⸨⸩ in a
    let i: mut u64 = 0u64
    while i < width:
        if bytes⟦0⟧ = 255u8:
            ※ a call handed the view, whose answer points nowhere
            return ⊥ why_at(bytes, 0)
        kids ⧺← [grown(bytes⟦1…#bytes⟧, levels - 1u64, width, a)?, Tree(.name ← "n" ⧺ ⍕i in a)]
        seen⸨i⸩ ← i
        i ← i + 1u64
    ※ one written over, which stays a value
    kids⟦0⟧ ← Tree(.name ← "first")
    Tree(.kids ← kids)

※ How many leaves and names a tree has, and what its leaves add up to.
fn counted(t: &Tree) → 〈u64, u64〉:
    match t⌖:
        u64(n):
            〈1u64, n〉
        str(_):
            〈1u64, 0u64〉
        [Tree](kids):
            let count: mut u64 = 0u64
            let sum: mut u64 = 0u64
            foreach &k: Tree = kids:
                let c: 〈u64, u64〉 = counted(k)
                count ← count + c⟦0⟧
                sum ← sum + c⟦1⟧
            〈count, sum〉

※ The tree written out onto `into`, which is `a`'s: a byte for each leaf and
※ name, and brackets around the kids.
fn spelled(t: &Tree, into: mut [u8] in a, a: &mut arena) → [u8] in a:
    match t⌖:
        [Tree](kids):
            into ⧺← ⟦91u8⟧
            foreach &k: Tree = kids:
                into ← spelled(k, into, a)
            into ⧺← ⟦93u8⟧
        u64(_):
            into ⧺← ⟦108u8⟧
        str(_):
            into ⧺← ⟦110u8⟧
    into

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let pool: mut arena = ⎕arena
    let bytes: u8⟦4⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8, 3u8, 4u8⟧ in ⎕static
    match grown(bytes, 3u64, 3u64, &mut pool):
        Tree(t):
            ※ three levels of three kids, each beside a name, the first of each
            ※ list written over with a name: four names and two trees a level,
            ※ 4 + 2 × (4 + 2 × (4 + 2 × 1)) things, the leaves at the bottom four
            let c: 〈u64, u64〉 = counted(&t)
            if c⟦0⟧ ≠ 36u64:
                return 1u6
            if c⟦1⟧ ≠ 32u64:
                return 2u6
            let text: [u8] = spelled(&t, [] in pool, &mut pool)
            ※ 36 leaves and names, and a pair of brackets for each of the 1 + 2 + 4
            ※ lists of kids
            if #text ≠ 36 + 14:
                return 8u6
        ⊥(_):
            return 3u6
    ※ a list joined onto one of the arena's and changed afterwards
    let inner: mut [Tree] = [Tree(.leaf ← 1u64)] in pool
    let outer: mut [Tree] = [] in pool
    outer ⧺← [Tree(.kids ← inner)]
    inner ⧺← [Tree(.leaf ← 2u64)]
    match outer⟦0⟧:
        [Tree](kept):
            if #kept ≠ 1:
                return 4u6
        _:
            return 5u6
    let refused: u8⟦2⟧ = ⟦255u8, 1u8⟧ in ⎕static
    match grown(refused, 2u64, 2u64, &mut pool):
        Tree(_):
            6u6
        ⊥(why):
            if why = Why.odd: 0u6 else: 7u6
